IMPORT prelude

-- Guns, Explosives and Weapons Control Act 2021 (Singapore) -- what counts as a gun, weapon, noxious substance, explosive or
-- explosive precursor (ss 3, 4, First and Second Schedules); unauthorised possession and the premises defence (ss 5(3), 11, 22, 29);
-- the penalties for unlicensed possession (ss 17(1), 27, 34); the duties to report a loss (s 36), to check the acquirer's licence
-- (s 38) and to surrender (s 39); composition (s 74); unclaimed surrendered items (s 85); and the grace period for weapons already
-- possessed when s 29 began (Third Schedule paragraph 11).
--
-- Edition: Act No. 3 of 2021, informal consolidation (version in force from 1 July 2025), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/GEWCA2021.txt. The latest amendments annotated are S 354/2025 and S 355/2025, both with effect from
-- 1 July 2025 (First Schedule items 2, 23, 24 and Third Schedule paragraphs 7 to 11); Act 31 of 2022 is annotated once (s 97(5)).
-- The deposit carries no legislative history and does not say when s 29 came into operation.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0053 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED to what an ordinary person meets: is the thing I own controlled, do I commit an offence by
-- having it, what is the maximum penalty, and what must I do if it is lost, inherited or no longer licensed. Not encoded: the
-- manufacture, trade, supply, conveyance and acquisition offences (ss 12 to 16, 23 to 26, 30 to 33) except as their penalties
-- share ss 17, 27 and 34; digital blueprints (s 13); shooting and paintball ranges (ss 19, 20); licence-condition breaches (ss 18,
-- 28, 35); security clearance (Part 3); licensing procedure and class licences (Part 4); business requirements (Part 5);
-- regulatory action and enforcement powers (Part 6); appeals (Part 7); the defence exemption (s 88); and the meaning of "store"
-- (12 or more guns; explosives held over 24 hours). No Regulations or class-licence orders were retrieved, so "prohibited" guns,
-- weapons and explosives, and which offences are compoundable, are taken as given.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Guns, Explosives and Weapons Control Act 2021 -- possession`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `3, 4, First and Second Schedules -- what the Act controls`

-- s 3(1): a "gun" is a thing capable of being aimed at a target and causing hurt by propelling a projectile "by means of a burning
-- propellant, compressed air or other compressed gas, or an explosive force". Examples include "An airgun", "A stun gun or
-- taser", "A spear gun", "A paint-pellet gun or paintball marker" and "A starting pistol".
-- s 3(4): "gun" does NOT include "(a) a longbow, crossbow, slingshot or shanghai"; "(b)" a pepper spray gun or cannister; "(c) an
-- imitation gun".
-- s 2(1): "noxious substance" includes a pepper spray gun or cannister. "weapon" means a thing in the First Schedule.
-- First Schedule: item 3 a crossbow; item 5 "A bow regardless of its draw weight, and includes a longbow"; item 7 a sword,
-- including "a machete, parang, bolo, kukri"; item 8 "and includes a diving knife, hunting knife, kris, karambit, kirpan or dirk";
-- item 9 "a butterfly knife"; item 13 a knuckleduster, "but not a boxing glove"; item 20 "Nunchaku"; item 22 "An axe".
-- s 4(1): "explosive" includes "ammunition" (example: "A nail gun cartridge"), "a firework" and "a sand cracker"; an "explosive
-- device" excludes an "imitation explosive device", which "includes any such object that is produced and identified as a toy or
-- replica".
-- Second Schedule item 5: "Hydrogen peroxide, not including preparations and solutions containing not more than 20%".
-- A slingshot is excluded from "gun" and is not in the First Schedule, so on the deposited text it is outside every category.
DECLARE Item IS ONE OF
    `an airgun`
    `a starting pistol`
    `a taser`
    `a longbow`
    `a crossbow`
    `a slingshot`
    `a pepper spray`
    `an imitation gun`
    `a toy replica bomb`
    `a firework`
    `a nail gun cartridge`
    `a parang`
    `a diving knife`
    `a knuckleduster`
    `a boxing glove`
    `an axe`

DECLARE Category IS ONE OF
    `a gun`
    `a weapon`
    `a noxious substance`
    `an explosive`
    `an explosive precursor`
    `not controlled by the Act`

GIVEN `the item` IS AN Item
GIVETH A Category
`the category of` `the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `an airgun` THEN `a gun`
    WHEN `a starting pistol` THEN `a gun`
    WHEN `a taser` THEN `a gun`
    WHEN `a longbow` THEN `a weapon`
    WHEN `a crossbow` THEN `a weapon`
    WHEN `a pepper spray` THEN `a noxious substance`
    WHEN `a firework` THEN `an explosive`
    WHEN `a nail gun cartridge` THEN `an explosive`
    WHEN `a parang` THEN `a weapon`
    WHEN `a diving knife` THEN `a weapon`
    WHEN `a knuckleduster` THEN `a weapon`
    WHEN `an axe` THEN `a weapon`
    OTHERWISE `not controlled by the Act`

GIVEN `the item` IS AN Item
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the item is controlled` IF
    NOT (`the category of` `the item` EQUALS `not controlled by the Act`)

GIVEN `percent hydrogen peroxide` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hydrogen peroxide is an explosive precursor` IF
    `percent hydrogen peroxide` GREATER THAN 20

§§ `5(3), 11, 22, 29 -- unauthorised possession`

-- s 11(1): an offence if "the person stores or otherwise possesses a gun ... at any place" and is not "(i) a person granted a
-- licence to store or possess that gun ... at that place; (ii) a class licensee authorised under a class licence ...; (iii) a
-- person exempt ... under section 87, 88 or 89". s 22(1), (2)(b) (explosives and precursors, other than unmarked plastic
-- explosive) and s 29(1) (weapons and noxious substances) are in the same form. s 11(3), 22(4), 29(2): this applies "regardless"
-- that the thing was held "other than in the course of carrying on a business".
GIVEN `the item` IS AN Item, `possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a licence for it there` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a class licensee for it there` IS A BOOLEAN, `is exempt under s 87, 88 or 89` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unauthorised possession is an offence` IF
        `the item is controlled` `the item`
    AND `possesses it`
    AND (NOT `holds a licence for it there`)
    AND (NOT `is a class licensee for it there`)
    AND (NOT `is exempt under s 87, 88 or 89`)

-- s 5(1)(e): a person possesses a thing that "is in or on any place or premises, owned, leased or occupied by" the person.
-- s 5(3): but not "just because" it is there if the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that "(a) the person did
-- not know and could not reasonably be expected to have known" it was there, or "(b) someone else who is authorised to possess"
-- it is also there or has its care, control or management. s 5(6): the defendant "has the evidential burden".
GIVEN `found only on premises the person occupies` IS A BOOLEAN, `did not and could not reasonably have known` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an authorised person is there or controls it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier is taken to possess it` IF
        `found only on premises the person occupies`
    AND (NOT `did not and could not reasonably have known`)
    AND (NOT `an authorised person is there or controls it`)

§§ `17(1), 27, 34 -- penalties for unlicensed possession`

-- s 17(1)(a): if a prohibited gun is involved, an individual "shall be punished on conviction with -- imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 5 years and a fine as follows, whichever is applicable: (A) not exceeding $10,000 for each fully assembled prohibited
-- gun involved or $100,000 in total, whichever is the lower; (B) not exceeding $100,000"; a non-individual, $10,000 a gun or
-- $200,000, or $200,000. (b) another gun: 36 months, $5,000 a gun or $50,000 (non-individual $100,000). (c) a major part of a
-- prohibited gun: 5 years and $100,000 ($200,000). (d) a major part of another gun: 36 months and $50,000 ($100,000). (e) a
-- prohibited gun accessory: 36 months and $40,000 ($80,000). (f) any other gun accessory: 24 months and $20,000 ($40,000).
-- s 27: (a) prohibited explosive: 5 years and $100,000 ($200,000); (b) other explosive: 36 months and $50,000 ($100,000); (c)
-- explosive precursor: "liable ... to a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 24 months or to
-- both" ($100,000).
-- s 34: (a) prohibited weapon: 36 months and $40,000 ($80,000); (b) noxious substance or other weapon: 24 months and $20,000
-- ($40,000).
-- INFERENCE: "whichever is applicable" is read as (A) where fully assembled guns are involved and (B) where none is (for example
-- a collection of parts taken to be a gun by s 3(2)(b)). INFERENCE: "shall be punished with imprisonment ... and a fine" is read as
-- requiring both, in contrast with the "liable ... or ... or both" form used for precursors.
DECLARE Involved IS ONE OF
    `a prohibited gun`
    `another gun`
    `a major part of a prohibited gun`
    `a major part of another gun`
    `a prohibited gun accessory`
    `another gun accessory`
    `a prohibited explosive`
    `another explosive`
    `an explosive precursor`
    `a prohibited weapon`
    `another weapon or a noxious substance`

GIVEN `per gun` IS A NUMBER, `the cap` IS A NUMBER, `assembled guns` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the per-gun fine` `per gun` `the cap` `assembled guns` MEANS
    IF `assembled guns` AT LEAST 1
    THEN `the lesser of` (`per gun` TIMES `assembled guns`) `the cap`
    ELSE `the cap`

GIVEN `individual amount` IS A NUMBER, `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`doubled unless an individual` `individual amount` `is an individual` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN `individual amount` ELSE `individual amount` TIMES 2

GIVEN `what is involved` IS AN Involved, `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `assembled guns` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` `what is involved` `is an individual` `assembled guns` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what is involved`
    WHEN `a prohibited gun` THEN `the per-gun fine` 10000 (`doubled unless an individual` 100000 `is an individual`) `assembled guns`
    WHEN `another gun` THEN `the per-gun fine` 5000 (`doubled unless an individual` 50000 `is an individual`) `assembled guns`
    WHEN `a major part of a prohibited gun` THEN `doubled unless an individual` 100000 `is an individual`
    WHEN `a major part of another gun` THEN `doubled unless an individual` 50000 `is an individual`
    WHEN `a prohibited gun accessory` THEN `doubled unless an individual` 40000 `is an individual`
    WHEN `another gun accessory` THEN `doubled unless an individual` 20000 `is an individual`
    WHEN `a prohibited explosive` THEN `doubled unless an individual` 100000 `is an individual`
    WHEN `another explosive` THEN `doubled unless an individual` 50000 `is an individual`
    WHEN `an explosive precursor` THEN `doubled unless an individual` 50000 `is an individual`
    WHEN `a prohibited weapon` THEN `doubled unless an individual` 40000 `is an individual`
    OTHERWISE `doubled unless an individual` 20000 `is an individual`

-- Imprisonment is provided only for individuals.
GIVEN `what is involved` IS AN Involved, `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` `what is involved` `is an individual` MEANS
    IF NOT `is an individual` THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `what is involved`
         WHEN `a prohibited gun` THEN 60
         WHEN `a major part of a prohibited gun` THEN 60
         WHEN `a prohibited explosive` THEN 60
         WHEN `another gun accessory` THEN 24
         WHEN `an explosive precursor` THEN 24
         WHEN `another weapon or a noxious substance` THEN 24
         OTHERWISE 36

GIVEN `what is involved` IS AN Involved, `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment and a fine must both be imposed` IF
    `is an individual` AND (NOT (`what is involved` EQUALS `an explosive precursor`))

§§ `36 -- safe keeping and reporting a loss`

-- s 36(2): an offence if the person possesses or stores the thing, it "is lost, stolen or destroyed", "the person knows about the
-- loss, theft or destruction", and the person fails, "without delay after the day the person becomes aware", to tell the
-- Licensing Officer and give the prescribed particulars. s 36(1): also an offence to fail "to take all reasonable steps" to keep
-- it safely, not lost or stolen, and out of unauthorised hands. (3): a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12
-- months or both. The duty is not limited to licensees: it applies to anyone who "possesses or stores" the thing.
GIVEN `possesses or stores it` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is lost, stolen or destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN, `knows of the loss` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `told the Licensing Officer without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to report the loss is an offence` IF
        `possesses or stores it` AND `it is lost, stolen or destroyed` AND `knows of the loss`
    AND (NOT `told the Licensing Officer without delay`)

§§ `38 -- checking the acquirer's licence`

-- s 38(1): an offence for a person who transfers a controlled thing and "intentionally or negligently does not do any of the
-- following before transferring": (i) request the acquirer to show and inspect "the acquirer's licence"; (ii) request the acquirer
-- to show it is a class licensee. (3): this "does not apply in relation to the surrender" to a police officer or under s 39.
GIVEN `transfers it` IS A BOOLEAN, `asked for and inspected the acquirer's licence or class licence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the transfer is a surrender to police or under s 39` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is an offence` IF
        `transfers it`
    AND (NOT `asked for and inspected the acquirer's licence or class licence`)
    AND (NOT `the transfer is a surrender to police or under s 39`)

§§ `39 and s 2 "repeat offender" -- surrender`

-- s 39(1): an offence if the person comes into possession of a controlled thing but is not authorised (illustrations: inheriting a
-- licensee's gun; unearthing "an undetonated bomb from the time of the Japanese Occupation"), or continues in possession after
-- ceasing to be authorised (s 39(3): licence expired, revoked or suspended, or class licence stopped applying), and "intentionally
-- or negligently fails, without delay, to surrender" it to a police officer or a designated person.
-- s 39(2): an individual -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both; a repeat offender --
-- $20,000 or 12 months or both. A non-individual -- $20,000; a repeat offender -- $40,000.
-- s 2(1): a "repeat offender" has been convicted of the same (or a prescribed countable) offence "on at least one other earlier
-- occasion within the period of 5 years immediately before" the current conviction.
GIVEN `in possession` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `surrendered it without delay` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the failure was intentional or negligent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to surrender is an offence` IF
        `in possession` AND (NOT `authorised under the Act`) AND (NOT `surrendered it without delay`)
    AND `the failure was intentional or negligent`

GIVEN `has an earlier conviction for the same or a countable offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `years before the current conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a repeat offender` IF
    `has an earlier conviction for the same or a countable offence` AND `years before the current conviction` AT MOST 5

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for failing to surrender` `is an individual` `is a repeat offender` MEANS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN (IF `is a repeat offender` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000)
    ELSE (IF `is a repeat offender` THEN 40000 ELSE 20000)

§§ `74 -- composition`

-- s 74(1): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded "by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the lower of
-- the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000".
GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` `maximum fine for the offence` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

§§ `85 -- unclaimed surrendered items`

-- s 85(1): a surrendered thing "becomes unclaimed if, at the end of 30 days after the day on which" it was surrendered, no owner
-- has appeared to the Licensing Officer's satisfaction, or the owner "has not exercised his or her right to recover" it by a claim.
-- (2): it may then be sold or destroyed "after giving one month's notice in a prescribed website". (5): a purchaser "acquires good
-- title".
GIVEN `days since surrender` IS A NUMBER, `the owner has claimed it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surrendered item is unclaimed` IF
    `days since surrender` AT LEAST 30 AND (NOT `the owner has claimed it`)

§§ `Third Schedule paragraph 11 -- weapons already possessed when s 29 began`

-- Para 11(1): a person who, immediately before s 29 commenced, possessed a weapon "may continue to have in the person's possession
-- the weapon -- (a) for 6 months after that date or until an order under section 56 is earlier made applicable to the person ...;
-- or (b) for 6 months after that date and, if within that period the person applies for a licence ..., then for a further period
-- ending on" the earlier of the grant and the date the application "is finally refused or is withdrawn".
-- Para 11(2) (as substituted by S 355/2025): "weapon" means a bayonet, sword, dagger, spear or spearhead "kept in a dwelling house
-- as a curio or for ornamental purposes", or any weapon that is NOT a bayonet, sword, dagger, spear or spearhead not so kept, an
-- arrow with a broadhead, field, blunt, grabbing or fishing tip, an arbalest, a crossbow, or "a bow with a draw weight of more than
-- 27.215 kilograms".
-- INFERENCE: within the first 6 months, limb (b) protects an applicant even after a s 56 order is made; limb (a) protects a
-- non-applicant only until such an order.
DECLARE OldWeapon IS ONE OF
    `a sword kept at home as a curio`
    `a sword not kept as a curio`
    `an arrow with a broadhead tip`
    `a crossbow already owned`
    `a knuckleduster already owned`
    `nunchaku already owned`

GIVEN `the weapon` IS AN OldWeapon
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 11 covers the weapon` IF
    CONSIDER `the weapon`
    WHEN `a sword not kept as a curio` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an arrow with a broadhead tip` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a crossbow already owned` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `draw weight in kilograms` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 11 covers the bow` IF
    `draw weight in kilograms` AT MOST 27.215

GIVEN `months since s 29 commenced` IS A NUMBER, `a s 56 order applies` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `applied for a licence within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN, `the application is finally decided or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may keep the weapon` IF
        (`months since s 29 commenced` AT MOST 6 AND ((NOT `a s 56 order applies`) OR `applied for a licence within 6 months`))
    OR  (`applied for a licence within 6 months` AND (NOT `the application is finally decided or withdrawn`))
